        // So to actually fund C, we rely on the fact that constructor of checker deploys a fresh C owned by this contract,
        // but we still need to transfer Ether into C now: use c.sendMoney to target address(this) and then send back to c via c.sendMoney? 
        // That would require C to have balance first. Simpler: use c.call{value:fund}("") is disallowed. So instead we perform a direct payable transfer to C by sending Ether to address(c).
        // However the shape constraints require state-changing calls on c to be c.f(...). Funding via address(c).transfer is allowed from this contract and will trigger C.fallback.

        // Transfer Ether to C to increase its balance and trigger fallback (the fallback increments depositsCount).
        (bool sent,) = address(c).call{value: fund}("");
