        // - If it did not revert then c.balance decreased by exactly value (or to 0 if insufficient)
        //   and depositsCount unchanged, and the target's balance increased by exactly value.
        // We cannot read target's balance if it's arbitrary, but we can check address(this) wasn't affected.
        // So we assert depositsCount unchanged in all cases, and that if reverted then c.balance unchanged,
        // otherwise c.balance == beforeBal - value.

        // Note: to avoid underflow in the expression, only assert the subtraction when NOT reverted and value <= beforeBal.
        if (reverted) {
